{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Got in a little [D]trouble down at county seat
[D]Lord they put me in the jailhouse [A]for loafin' on the street[D]
[D]When the judge read the verdict  I was a guilty man
[D]Said 45 dollars [A]or 40 days in the [D]can
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Said that'll be [G]cash on the barrelhead, [D]son
[D]You can make your [A]choice if you're twenty [D][D7]one
No money [G]down, no credit [D]plan
No time to [A7]chase you 'cause I'm a busy man[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Forty days in the jailhouse, four days on the road
I was a-feeling mighty hungry, my feet a heavy load
Saw a Greyhound coming', stuck out my thumb
Before I got to my seat, the driver caught my arm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Said that'll be cash on the barrelhead son
This old grey dog gets paid to run
When the engine starts and the wheels all roll
Give me cash on the barrelhead, I'll take you down the road
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Said that'll be cash on the barrelhead son
You can make your choice if you're twenty one
No money down, no credit plan
No time to chase you 'cause I'm a busy man
{end_of_verse}
